WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.536
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:08.793
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:15.449
Unit two: Simple Directions. In this unit, you will ask for and give simple directions.

4
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.172
Left.

5
00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:20.940
Left means the side of your body where your heart is.

6
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.717
Turn left at the bank.

7
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:26.395
Your turn. Say: Left.

8
00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:29.805
Left.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:31.644
Right.

10
00:00:32.344 --> 00:00:34.541
Right means the opposite side to left.

11
00:00:34.841 --> 00:00:36.190
The park is on the right.

12
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.995
Your turn. Say: Right.

13
00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:43.417
Right.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.290
Straight.

15
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.733
Straight means going forward, not turning.

16
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.765
Go straight for two blocks.

17
00:00:51.465 --> 00:00:54.234
Your turn. Say: Straight.

18
00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:57.888
Straight.

19
00:00:58.883 --> 00:00:59.583
Turn.

20
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.166
Turn means to change direction.

21
00:01:02.466 --> 00:01:04.349
Turn right at the corner.

22
00:01:05.049 --> 00:01:07.551
Your turn. Say: Turn.

23
00:01:10.251 --> 00:01:11.031
Turn.

24
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:13.157
Next to.

25
00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:16.751
Next to means very close, at the side of something.

26
00:01:17.051 --> 00:01:18.934
The school is next to the market.

27
00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.960
Your turn. Say: Next to.

28
00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.556
Next to.

29
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.412
Between.

30
00:01:29.112 --> 00:01:31.297
Between means in the middle of two things.

31
00:01:31.597 --> 00:01:34.224
The bank is between the shop and the park.

32
00:01:34.924 --> 00:01:37.564
Your turn. Say: Between.

33
00:01:40.264 --> 00:01:41.080
Between.

34
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:42.783
North.

35
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:46.097
North means the direction at the top of a map.

36
00:01:46.397 --> 00:01:48.420
Laos is north of Cambodia.

37
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.865
Your turn. Say: North.

38
00:01:54.565 --> 00:01:55.311
North.

39
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:57.225
South.

40
00:01:57.925 --> 00:02:00.621
South means the direction at the bottom of a map.

41
00:02:00.921 --> 00:02:02.804
The sea is south of Phnom Penh.

42
00:02:03.504 --> 00:02:06.180
Your turn. Say: South.

43
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:09.649
South.

44
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:11.326
East.

45
00:02:12.026 --> 00:02:14.711
East means the direction where the sun comes up.

46
00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:16.917
The sun rises in the east.

47
00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:19.956
Your turn. Say: East.

48
00:02:22.656 --> 00:02:23.332
East.

49
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:24.795
West.

50
00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:28.691
West means the direction where the sun goes down.

51
00:02:28.991 --> 00:02:30.654
The sun sets in the west.

52
00:02:31.354 --> 00:02:34.134
Your turn. Say: West.

53
00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:37.672
West.

54
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:39.754
Roundabout.

55
00:02:40.454 --> 00:02:44.033
Roundabout means a round place where several roads meet.

56
00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:45.995
Go around the roundabout.

57
00:02:46.695 --> 00:02:49.719
Your turn. Say: Roundabout.

58
00:02:52.419 --> 00:02:53.328
Roundabout.

59
00:02:54.317 --> 00:02:55.527
Signpost.

60
00:02:56.227 --> 00:02:59.503
Signpost means a sign that shows the way to places.

61
00:02:59.803 --> 00:03:01.211
Look at the signpost.

62
00:03:01.911 --> 00:03:04.830
Your turn. Say: Signpost.

63
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.508
Signpost.

64
00:03:09.517 --> 00:03:11.667
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:15.119
Excuse me, Ms. Sarah. Where is the library?

66
00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:19.032
Go straight and turn left at the roundabout.

67
00:03:20.317 --> 00:03:21.840
Is it next to the bank?

68
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:26.206
No, it is between the post office and the park.

69
00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:28.924
Thank you very much!

70
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:33.182
You're welcome. Look at the signpost!

71
00:03:34.483 --> 00:03:37.818
Grammar focus: Imperatives for directions.

72
00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:41.621
Turn left. Go straight. Turn right at the corner.

73
00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:46.129
Start with the verb when you give directions. Add 'please' to be polite.

74
00:03:47.117 --> 00:03:50.036
Now read and listen. The Way to School.

75
00:03:50.336 --> 00:03:52.591
Every morning, I walk to school.

76
00:03:53.883 --> 00:03:57.334
I go straight along my street and turn left at the roundabout.

77
00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.520
Then I turn right at the signpost.

78
00:04:02.817 --> 00:04:06.256
My school is next to the market, between the bank and the park.

79
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.606
It takes ten minutes, and I never get lost!

80
00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:14.697
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:14.997 --> 00:04:16.485
blank left at the bank.

82
00:04:16.785 --> 00:04:20.137
A, Turn. B, Turns. C, Turning.

83
00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.359
The answer is A: Turn.

84
00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.687
The sun rises in the blank.

85
00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:33.455
A, west. B, east. C, south.

86
00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.368
The answer is B: east.

87
00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:43.463
The bank is blank the shop and the park.

88
00:04:43.763 --> 00:04:47.057
A, between. B, on. C, under.

89
00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.224
The answer is A: between.

90
00:04:54.717 --> 00:04:58.623
Now it's your turn to speak. Give directions from your house to your school.

91
00:05:03.923 --> 00:05:09.701
Go straight along my street. Turn left at the market. The school is next to the temple.

92
00:05:10.001 --> 00:05:11.606
Excellent answer, Rithy!

93
00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:17.672
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and imperatives for directions.

94
00:05:17.972 --> 00:05:21.832
Today's value is helpfulness. Help your friends and neighbours.

95
00:05:22.132 --> 00:05:24.517
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

96
00:05:24.817 --> 00:05:27.830
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

